I included neither of the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. Neither is granted, and the target has no WASI adapter. Adding either would exceed the node's authority. If operations needs them, the graph's `with` clause would have to grant those capabilities explicitly.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The channel stamps the session identity and delivery status itself;
        // return its confirmation unchanged rather than fabricating either field.
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

